417] [17592186530379 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530379 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530379 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186529918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530379 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dc482d57-60ea-5929-a93c-02bf101b157d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1077 "field-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186529577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530382 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ddb27815-0b88-5fe1-9bd9-3f33b06ca48a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-8x(t)+3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-6x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "21116522-1e68-5aeb-8229-3d0039b396bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530434 #edb/ref 1074 "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=2x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=2x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/33/330e2a1dd9f7d2cbcadb61fe49e767d95ee76a2cb669a9917ef3f6333719b98f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333345" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/51/51ffadb1da41e6a1fe06fdc9c14a6967d3a80b4d26c6a830a401105e0f18bbf5.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,2]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}.\n\nFinally, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector {{field-9}} as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is \n{{field-10}}.\n\nTherefore,\n{{field-11}} \n$<0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22670f3b-ee2e-505b-bc5c-db0616554dee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530436 #edb/ref 1074 "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=-2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/6e/6ea2d64a390187a28cfcd1c2692e97e5dc2ca5cb37649ba12cf71864e36958ea.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=2x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f2340cbff80765a5d3b551e87eb4207eebad05970e366ceeccd7bb142c0b677.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$\n\nSo, for this particular system, both eigenvalues are negative. The eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue) is the one closest to $0.$\n\nNow, since the solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ${v}_{1}$ as they move towards the origin, the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior is ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\n\nTherefore, ${\\lambda }_{2}<{\\lambda }_{1}<0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d325e43f-35f1-5542-8db8-397925f79316" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530527 #edb/ref 1074 "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/e5/e5c236defa66a00f12cd338ed0012cf91e4d7c15aa4865fc2b1edf5b0e2ea1da.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
